1
00:00:00,926 --> 00:00:00,910
Picture this.

2
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:03,570
You're stopped at a red
light in your new BYD.

3
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:05,610
The car behind you doesn't stop in time.

4
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:06,810
It's not a big crash.

5
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:07,810
Nobody's hurt.

6
00:00:07,860 --> 00:00:09,050
The bumper's pushed in,

7
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,930
a sensor light is flashing on the dash,

8
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:14,030
and you think: no worries, the
insurance will sort it out.

9
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:16,690
But this is where a very
different story begins.

10
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:18,290
Because for a lot of Australians,

11
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:21,790
the most stressful part of owning
a new electric car isn't the crash.

12
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,650
It's everything that happens after it.

13
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:26,350
The tow truck that has to take
the car somewhere special.

14
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,810
The repairer that isn't
certified to touch it.

15
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:30,950
The battery check nobody
can do on the spot.

16
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,150
The wait for parts.

17
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,470
And then, twelve months later,
the insurance renewal letter.

18
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:38,570
BYD is now one of the biggest
car brands in Australia.

19
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:40,830
Hundreds of thousands of
Aussies are driving one.

20
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:41,870
So in this video,

21
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:45,470
we're going to follow a BYD from the
moment of impact all the way to the next

22
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:49,510
insurance bill using real
2026 data from insurers,

23
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:52,410
repairers, actuaries and BYD itself.

24
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:53,550
No scare stories.

25
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,170
Just what actually happens.

26
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:56,250
And stay to the end,

27
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,330
because I'll give you a simple checklist
that could save you weeks of waiting

28
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:00,760
and a lot of money.

29
00:01:01,322 --> 00:01:03,892
First, why does this
matter so much right now?

30
00:01:03,942 --> 00:01:05,912
Because the numbers have changed fast.

31
00:01:05,962 --> 00:01:07,852
In September 2026,

32
00:01:07,902 --> 00:01:13,852
BYD sold 8,191 new cars in Australia
up sixty-one per cent on the same month

33
00:01:13,902 --> 00:01:14,692
last year.

34
00:01:14,742 --> 00:01:17,492
That made it the second
best-selling brand in the country,

35
00:01:17,542 --> 00:01:20,912
behind only Toyota, and it's second
for the year to date as well.

36
00:01:20,962 --> 00:01:25,512
Ford, Mazda, Kia, Hyundai BYD
is now outselling all of them.

37
00:01:25,562 --> 00:01:28,312
Its range now covers
almost every type of buyer:

38
00:01:28,362 --> 00:01:30,212
the Atto 1 and Dolphin city cars,

39
00:01:30,262 --> 00:01:33,512
the Atto 3 and Sealion 7 SUVs,

40
00:01:33,562 --> 00:01:38,012
the Seal sedan, the Sealion 6
plug-in hybrid, and the Shark 6 ute.

41
00:01:38,062 --> 00:01:41,712
At the same time, electric and
plug-in cars have gone mainstream.

42
00:01:41,762 --> 00:01:43,652
In September 2026,

43
00:01:43,702 --> 00:01:47,192
battery electric cars made up more than
twenty-four per cent of new car sales

44
00:01:47,242 --> 00:01:49,932
in Australia and for the
second month in a row,

45
00:01:49,982 --> 00:01:53,152
more pure electric cars were
sold than petrol-only cars.

46
00:01:53,202 --> 00:01:54,912
And insurers are seeing it.

47
00:01:54,962 --> 00:01:59,132
NRMA Insurance says requests for
electric vehicle insurance quotes were up

48
00:01:59,182 --> 00:02:02,552
eighty per cent in the
first nine months of 2026.

49
00:02:02,602 --> 00:02:05,612
More of these cars on the road
means more of them in crashes.

50
00:02:05,662 --> 00:02:07,412
That's not a criticism of BYD.

51
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:08,852
It's simply maths.

52
00:02:08,902 --> 00:02:12,632
And it means a lot of drivers are about
to discover how an EV crash repair

53
00:02:12,682 --> 00:02:15,002
actually works for the first time.

54
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,490
So let's go back to that red light.

55
00:02:17,540 --> 00:02:20,190
The first thing that happens
after a crash is the tow.

56
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:23,450
And with an electric car, even
that is a little different.

57
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:26,630
An EV has a large high-voltage
battery under the floor.

58
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:30,310
Most tow operators will want to move
it on a flatbed rather than dragging it

59
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:31,210
on its wheels,

60
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:34,970
and the car has to be handled in a
specific way so the drive system isn't

61
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:35,730
damaged.

62
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,210
If the battery might have been hit,

63
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:40,370
it can't just be parked next to
other cars in a holding yard.

64
00:02:40,420 --> 00:02:44,570
Many assessing centres now keep damaged
EVs in a separate quarantine area,

65
00:02:44,620 --> 00:02:45,450
away from buildings,

66
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:49,190
because of the small but serious
risk of a delayed battery fire.

67
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:52,270
Then comes the next question:
who's allowed to fix it?

68
00:02:52,320 --> 00:02:55,270
Repairing an electric car properly
needs trained technicians,

69
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:58,970
insulated tools, and procedures to
safely isolate the high-voltage system

70
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:01,310
before anyone starts cutting or welding.

71
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,750
Back in 2024,

72
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:06,470
the Motor Trades Association of Australia
said only around ten per cent of the

73
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:10,110
country's repairers were certified
to work on electric vehicles.

74
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,690
Its chief executive, Matt Hobbs,

75
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:15,210
pointed out that technicians have to
be trained to safely de-power systems

76
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:18,030
running at around four hundred
volts before they start work.

77
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:21,790
And a report by the association with
Deloitte found that only around forty-one

78
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:25,430
per cent of EV technician job
vacancies were being filled.

79
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:27,090
That number has been growing,

80
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:30,090
and BYD has its own approved
collision repair network.

81
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:31,670
But depending on where you live,

82
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:34,230
the nearest approved shop
could be a long way away.

83
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:36,190
So before a single panel is touched,

84
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,950
your car might already
have travelled further,

85
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,460
and waited longer, than a
petrol car with the same damage.

86
00:03:42,308 --> 00:03:44,198
Now the car arrives at the repairer.

87
00:03:44,248 --> 00:03:45,998
And this is where things get expensive,

88
00:03:46,048 --> 00:03:48,618
because modern cars hide
a lot behind the bumper.

89
00:03:48,668 --> 00:03:52,038
A rear bumper on a new BYD
isn't just a piece of plastic.

90
00:03:52,088 --> 00:03:53,898
It can carry parking sensors,

91
00:03:53,948 --> 00:03:57,278
a reversing camera and radar
units for the safety systems.

92
00:03:57,328 --> 00:03:58,198
After a hit,

93
00:03:58,248 --> 00:04:01,818
those sensors often need to be
replaced or at least recalibrated,

94
00:04:01,868 --> 00:04:04,858
and calibration needs
special equipment and time.

95
00:04:04,908 --> 00:04:08,398
A bump that would have cost a few hundred
dollars on a twenty-year-old car can

96
00:04:08,448 --> 00:04:10,338
turn into a bill of several thousand.

97
00:04:10,388 --> 00:04:11,638
Then there's the battery.

98
00:04:11,688 --> 00:04:12,688
Even if it looks fine,

99
00:04:12,738 --> 00:04:16,438
the repairer and the insurer need to
know whether the impact has damaged the

100
00:04:16,488 --> 00:04:18,538
pack or its protective casing.

101
00:04:18,588 --> 00:04:21,638
On some models, that means removing
the battery for inspection.

102
00:04:21,688 --> 00:04:24,598
And if the pack is damaged,
the cost can be huge.

103
00:04:24,648 --> 00:04:27,438
In a report published in April 2026,

104
00:04:27,488 --> 00:04:30,965
actuarial firm Taylor Fry said the
battery can make up around thirty to fifty

105
00:04:31,015 --> 00:04:33,318
per cent of an electric car's value.

106
00:04:33,368 --> 00:04:36,858
Replace the battery, and you may be
looking at most of the cost of the car.

107
00:04:36,908 --> 00:04:40,878
That's why some EVs with relatively
modest damage end up written off.

108
00:04:40,928 --> 00:04:42,678
Not because the car is destroyed,

109
00:04:42,728 --> 00:04:46,338
but because the risk and cost of repairing
the battery is too high compared to

110
00:04:46,388 --> 00:04:47,448
what the car is worth.

111
00:04:47,498 --> 00:04:51,258
Industry insiders have described cases
where electric cars were written off

112
00:04:51,308 --> 00:04:53,558
because the battery casing was scratched,

113
00:04:53,608 --> 00:04:57,318
even though the cells inside were probably
fine simply because nobody had the

114
00:04:57,368 --> 00:05:00,318
diagnostic information to
prove the pack was safe.

115
00:05:00,368 --> 00:05:03,858
And when an insurer writes off
an EV, it doesn't get much back.

116
00:05:03,908 --> 00:05:08,278
In 2024, an assessing industry manager
said the salvage value of a written-off

117
00:05:08,328 --> 00:05:12,078
electric car was only around eight to
ten per cent of its replacement value,

118
00:05:12,128 --> 00:05:15,898
because there was so little demand
for used EV batteries and parts.

119
00:05:15,948 --> 00:05:19,558
Every one of those write-offs is a cost
that ends up spread across everyone's

120
00:05:19,608 --> 00:05:20,338
premiums.

121
00:05:20,388 --> 00:05:23,458
To be clear, not every
insurer sees it the same way.

122
00:05:23,508 --> 00:05:24,718
Allianz, for example,

123
00:05:24,768 --> 00:05:28,598
has said that cosmetic EV repairs
generally take about as long as petrol car

124
00:05:28,648 --> 00:05:32,598
repairs, and that it had no data
showing EVs are written off more often.

125
00:05:32,648 --> 00:05:36,138
The problem is concentrated in the
serious crashes the ones that reach the

126
00:05:36,188 --> 00:05:38,148
battery and the high-voltage system.

127
00:05:38,906 --> 00:05:42,416
To be fair to BYD, its
battery design does help here.

128
00:05:42,466 --> 00:05:46,936
BYD uses what it calls the Blade
battery, a lithium iron phosphate design.

129
00:05:46,986 --> 00:05:48,616
Back in 2024,

130
00:05:48,666 --> 00:05:52,556
BYD Australia's collision and repair
representatives explained that the Blade

131
00:05:52,606 --> 00:05:54,316
battery is built in a way that can,

132
00:05:54,366 --> 00:05:55,056
in some cases,

133
00:05:55,106 --> 00:05:59,656
allow damaged sections to be repaired
rather than replacing the whole pack.

134
00:05:59,706 --> 00:06:03,536
Lithium iron phosphate cells are also
generally considered more stable and

135
00:06:03,586 --> 00:06:06,996
less prone to thermal runaway than
some other battery chemistries.

136
00:06:07,046 --> 00:06:08,936
That's genuinely good news for owners.

137
00:06:08,986 --> 00:06:11,636
But it only helps if the
repairer is trained to do it,

138
00:06:11,686 --> 00:06:15,196
has the parts, and the insurer
agrees that a repair is safe.

139
00:06:15,246 --> 00:06:18,886
And that brings us to the part
almost every BYD owner talks about.

140
00:06:20,403 --> 00:06:20,969
The wait.

141
00:06:21,019 --> 00:06:23,449
In the early years of BYD in Australia,

142
00:06:23,499 --> 00:06:26,629
parts delays were one of the most
common complaints in owner groups.

143
00:06:26,679 --> 00:06:30,489
Some owners publicly described waiting
months for crash parts while their cars

144
00:06:30,539 --> 00:06:31,949
sat at the repairer.

145
00:06:31,999 --> 00:06:35,529
BYD's own executives have acknowledged
that the brand had a reputation for

146
00:06:35,579 --> 00:06:38,389
slow parts and service, and
that it needed to fix it.

147
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:43,169
And in 2026, BYD has spent serious
money trying to do exactly that.

148
00:06:43,219 --> 00:06:48,509
In October, BYD Australia said it now
holds more than 580,000 parts for BYD

149
00:06:48,559 --> 00:06:50,149
and Denza models locally,

150
00:06:50,199 --> 00:06:53,029
covering around ninety-five
per cent of what dealers need,

151
00:06:53,079 --> 00:06:57,389
worth more than twenty-five million
dollars, across warehouses in four cities.

152
00:06:57,439 --> 00:07:00,449
It says it now stocks Blade
battery packs locally too,

153
00:07:00,499 --> 00:07:04,169
and that parts not in stock can be sent
by air freight rather than waiting for

154
00:07:04,219 --> 00:07:05,009
a ship.

155
00:07:05,059 --> 00:07:07,589
To put that ninety-five
per cent in context:

156
00:07:07,639 --> 00:07:09,229
back in 2024,

157
00:07:09,279 --> 00:07:13,429
MG told CarAdvice its own parts fill
rate was around ninety-one per cent,

158
00:07:13,479 --> 00:07:16,889
with air-freighted parts taking about
two working weeks when they weren't in

159
00:07:16,939 --> 00:07:18,129
stock locally.

160
00:07:18,179 --> 00:07:21,489
Polestar said overseas parts
could take four to six weeks.

161
00:07:21,539 --> 00:07:22,829
So on paper,

162
00:07:22,879 --> 00:07:27,649
BYD's 2026 parts promise is now among
the strongest of the newer brands.

163
00:07:27,699 --> 00:07:31,429
The real test is whether owners waiting
on crash repairs actually feel the

164
00:07:31,479 --> 00:07:32,389
difference.

165
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:33,689
What about servicing?

166
00:07:33,739 --> 00:07:37,489
In a September 2026 interview
with NRMA's Open Road,

167
00:07:37,539 --> 00:07:41,429
BYD said the average wait for a
service booking was about seven days,

168
00:07:41,479 --> 00:07:44,009
and that it was aiming to bring
that down to four or five.

169
00:07:44,059 --> 00:07:47,009
But the wider industry still
has a capacity problem.

170
00:07:47,059 --> 00:07:48,809
In July 2026,

171
00:07:48,859 --> 00:07:52,749
a review commissioned by the Australian
Automotive Dealer Association found

172
00:07:52,799 --> 00:07:56,589
that some workshops had backlogs of
six to eight weeks just to diagnose a

173
00:07:56,639 --> 00:07:59,309
problem especially on electric vehicles.

174
00:07:59,359 --> 00:08:01,149
So even with the parts on the shelf,

175
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:03,109
the bottleneck can move
to the workshop itself:

176
00:08:03,159 --> 00:08:06,089
not enough trained
people, not enough bays,

177
00:08:06,139 --> 00:08:07,999
and too many cars arriving at once.

178
00:08:08,793 --> 00:08:11,483
Quick pause before we get to
the money side of all this.

179
00:08:11,533 --> 00:08:15,263
If you drive a BYD, or any
EV, I want to hear from you.

180
00:08:15,313 --> 00:08:16,643
Have you had a crash repair?

181
00:08:16,693 --> 00:08:19,483
How long did it take, and how
did your insurer handle it?

182
00:08:19,533 --> 00:08:23,323
Tell me in the comments real experiences
help other Aussies far more than any

183
00:08:23,373 --> 00:08:24,183
brochure.

184
00:08:24,233 --> 00:08:25,183
And if you want honest,

185
00:08:25,233 --> 00:08:28,883
fact-checked videos about the
Australian car market, hit subscribe.

186
00:08:28,933 --> 00:08:31,393
It's free and it really
helps the channel grow.

187
00:08:32,165 --> 00:08:34,335
Now let's talk about who pays.

188
00:08:34,385 --> 00:08:36,035
According to the Insurance
Council of Australia,

189
00:08:36,085 --> 00:08:40,095
the average cost of motor vehicle repairs
has risen around twenty-six per cent

190
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:44,795
since 2022, and repair costs now account
for roughly sixty per cent of the

191
00:08:44,845 --> 00:08:47,055
money insurers pay out on motor claims.

192
00:08:47,105 --> 00:08:49,915
That's across all cars, not just EVs.

193
00:08:49,965 --> 00:08:53,115
Sensors, cameras, more
expensive paint and panels,

194
00:08:53,165 --> 00:08:56,755
and a shortage of skilled labour
have all pushed the average bill up.

195
00:08:56,805 --> 00:08:58,255
Electric cars add another layer.

196
00:08:58,305 --> 00:09:02,555
A senior figure in BYD's own collision
repair network told an industry

197
00:09:02,605 --> 00:09:06,875
magazine that EV repairs currently sit
in a cost category more like high-end

198
00:09:06,925 --> 00:09:08,015
luxury cars.

199
00:09:08,065 --> 00:09:11,755
And when repairs cost more, insurers
have to charge more to cover the risk.

200
00:09:11,805 --> 00:09:13,535
There's also a hire car issue.

201
00:09:13,585 --> 00:09:17,115
While your car is off the road,
someone has to pay for a replacement.

202
00:09:17,165 --> 00:09:20,215
If the repair takes weeks,
that hire bill keeps running.

203
00:09:20,265 --> 00:09:22,735
And all of those costs
end up in the same place:

204
00:09:22,785 --> 00:09:24,825
the premiums everyone pays at renewal.

205
00:09:25,663 --> 00:09:30,123
So what has actually happened
to BYD insurance prices in 2026?

206
00:09:30,173 --> 00:09:33,233
In April 2026,

207
00:09:33,283 --> 00:09:36,853
insurance comparison site Compare the
Market published an analysis of premiums

208
00:09:36,903 --> 00:09:39,713
across popular hybrid and electric cars.

209
00:09:39,763 --> 00:09:43,073
It found that the average premium for
battery electric vehicles had risen

210
00:09:43,123 --> 00:09:45,333
about ten per cent
compared to a year earlier,

211
00:09:45,383 --> 00:09:49,153
to around two thousand three
hundred dollars a year.

212
00:09:49,203 --> 00:09:52,053
And for some BYD models,
the jump was bigger.

213
00:09:52,103 --> 00:09:55,793
The average quoted premium for the
Sealion 6 rose about eighteen per cent,

214
00:09:55,843 --> 00:10:01,993
from around $1,482 to around $1,821.

215
00:10:02,043 --> 00:10:04,033
The Dolphin went up about nine per cent,

216
00:10:04,083 --> 00:10:10,113
from around $1,437 to about $1,578.

217
00:10:10,163 --> 00:10:15,373
The Shark 6 rose about five
per cent, to around $2,172.

218
00:10:15,423 --> 00:10:19,053
And the Sealion 7 was almost
flat, up about half a per cent.

219
00:10:19,103 --> 00:10:21,483
Other research tells a similar story.

220
00:10:21,533 --> 00:10:27,173
CHOICE reported in January 2026 that
the average premium it found for EVs was

221
00:10:27,223 --> 00:10:29,973
about $2,545 a year,

222
00:10:30,023 --> 00:10:34,153
compared with about
$1,702 for petrol cars.

223
00:10:34,203 --> 00:10:35,483
And in the Taylor Fry report,

224
00:10:35,533 --> 00:10:39,493
the spread of quotes for an Atto 3
between the cheapest and most expensive

225
00:10:39,543 --> 00:10:45,753
insurer was around $900 compared with
roughly $500 for a petrol Mazda CX-30.

226
00:10:45,803 --> 00:10:46,973
Now, two important points.

227
00:10:47,023 --> 00:10:51,373
These are averages from specific
comparisons, not your personal quote.

228
00:10:51,423 --> 00:10:55,873
Your age, postcode, driving history
and excess all matter enormously.

229
00:10:55,923 --> 00:10:59,013
And BYD isn't the most
expensive brand to insure.

230
00:10:59,063 --> 00:11:01,593
In earlier comparisons, Teslas cost more.

231
00:11:01,643 --> 00:11:04,193
But the trend is clear:
for many EV owners,

232
00:11:04,243 --> 00:11:07,853
the cost of insurance is rising faster
than for the average petrol car.

233
00:11:07,903 --> 00:11:11,233
And that big gap between insurers means
shopping around has never mattered

234
00:11:11,283 --> 00:11:12,083
more.

235
00:11:12,624 --> 00:11:16,394
So you've had the crash, the car's at
the repairer, and nothing is happening.

236
00:11:16,444 --> 00:11:18,034
What can you actually do?

237
00:11:18,084 --> 00:11:20,954
First, know that your
insurer has rules to follow.

238
00:11:21,004 --> 00:11:24,354
Most Australian insurers have signed
up to the General Insurance Code of

239
00:11:24,404 --> 00:11:25,234
Practice.

240
00:11:25,284 --> 00:11:28,374
It sets out standards for
how claims should be handled.

241
00:11:28,424 --> 00:11:29,294
Under the code,

242
00:11:29,344 --> 00:11:32,834
insurers are generally expected to give
you a progress update at least every

243
00:11:32,884 --> 00:11:34,234
twenty business days,

244
00:11:34,284 --> 00:11:37,434
to respond to routine requests
within ten business days,

245
00:11:37,484 --> 00:11:41,234
and in most cases to make a decision
on your claim within four months.

246
00:11:41,284 --> 00:11:43,034
If you feel your claim is stuck,

247
00:11:43,084 --> 00:11:46,794
ask your insurer in writing for an
update and for a timeline and mention the

248
00:11:46,844 --> 00:11:47,814
code.

249
00:11:47,864 --> 00:11:49,994
Second, if you're not
happy with the answer,

250
00:11:50,044 --> 00:11:52,594
use the insurer's internal
complaints process.

251
00:11:52,644 --> 00:11:55,354
Put it in writing and keep
a record of every call.

252
00:11:55,404 --> 00:11:58,594
Insurers generally have thirty
days to respond to a complaint.

253
00:11:58,644 --> 00:11:59,874
If that doesn't resolve it,

254
00:11:59,924 --> 00:12:03,174
you can take your complaint to the
Australian Financial Complaints Authority,

255
00:12:03,224 --> 00:12:04,494
known as AFCA.

256
00:12:04,544 --> 00:12:07,234
It's free for consumers and
it's independent of the insurer.

257
00:12:07,284 --> 00:12:09,654
Before you go, gather everything:

258
00:12:09,704 --> 00:12:11,654
the claim number, your photos,

259
00:12:11,704 --> 00:12:15,094
the repairer's estimates, and
your diary of calls and emails.

260
00:12:15,144 --> 00:12:17,854
A clear timeline makes a
complaint much stronger.

261
00:12:17,904 --> 00:12:19,634
Third, if the delay is about parts,

262
00:12:19,684 --> 00:12:23,634
and not the insurer, remember
the Australian Consumer Law.

263
00:12:23,684 --> 00:12:27,194
Manufacturers and importers have to
make spare parts and repair facilities

264
00:12:27,244 --> 00:12:29,954
reasonably available
for a reasonable time.

265
00:12:30,004 --> 00:12:33,534
If the car is new and the problem
is a fault rather than crash damage,

266
00:12:33,584 --> 00:12:37,074
you also have consumer guarantee rights
against the business that sold it to

267
00:12:37,124 --> 00:12:37,694
you.

268
00:12:37,744 --> 00:12:39,784
Your state's fair trading office can help.

269
00:12:40,497 --> 00:12:42,387
So here's the checklist I promised.

270
00:12:42,437 --> 00:12:43,907
Save this one.

271
00:12:43,957 --> 00:12:46,247
Before a crash happens: check your policy.

272
00:12:46,297 --> 00:12:48,767
Does it cover a hire
car, and for how long?

273
00:12:48,817 --> 00:12:52,247
Is the hire car capped at a
dollar amount or a number of days?

274
00:12:52,297 --> 00:12:55,267
Can you choose your own repairer,
or does the insurer choose?

275
00:12:55,317 --> 00:12:59,607
And find out where your nearest
BYD-approved collision repairer actually is.

276
00:12:59,657 --> 00:13:02,627
When you renew: don't just
accept the renewal price.

277
00:13:02,677 --> 00:13:04,807
Get quotes from at least three insurers.

278
00:13:04,857 --> 00:13:08,267
With differences of hundreds of dollars
between companies for the same car,

279
00:13:08,317 --> 00:13:11,647
a twenty-minute search can pay
for itself many times over.

280
00:13:11,697 --> 00:13:13,867
Ask how they handle EV battery damage,

281
00:13:13,917 --> 00:13:16,787
and whether they have a
specialist EV claims process.

282
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:21,047
After a crash: take photos of everything,
including the dashboard warnings.

283
00:13:21,097 --> 00:13:24,407
Tell the tow operator it's an
electric or plug-in vehicle.

284
00:13:24,457 --> 00:13:28,287
Ask the insurer or repairer for a
written estimate of the timeline.

285
00:13:28,337 --> 00:13:31,447
Keep a diary of every call
and email, with dates.

286
00:13:31,497 --> 00:13:33,647
And if the car has been
hit near the battery,

287
00:13:33,697 --> 00:13:35,527
ask whether a battery
health check has been done,

288
00:13:35,577 --> 00:13:36,967
and get a copy of the result.

289
00:13:37,017 --> 00:13:39,527
And one more thing to
check on your policy:

290
00:13:39,577 --> 00:13:42,927
is your car insured for an
agreed value or a market value?

291
00:13:42,977 --> 00:13:46,627
With an agreed value, you and the
insurer settle on the amount up front.

292
00:13:46,677 --> 00:13:47,787
With market value,

293
00:13:47,837 --> 00:13:51,067
the insurer pays what the car is
worth at the time of the crash.

294
00:13:51,117 --> 00:13:53,567
If an EV is written off
because of battery damage,

295
00:13:53,617 --> 00:13:57,387
that difference can matter a lot
especially in a market where used EV prices

296
00:13:57,437 --> 00:13:58,567
have been falling.

297
00:13:58,617 --> 00:14:01,607
So read the policy wording,
not just the price.

298
00:14:01,657 --> 00:14:03,807
It's also worth knowing
who chooses the repairer.

299
00:14:03,857 --> 00:14:06,467
Some policies let you
pick your own workshop,

300
00:14:06,517 --> 00:14:09,087
while others send you to
the insurer's own network.

301
00:14:09,137 --> 00:14:12,487
If you want an EV-certified
or BYD-approved repairer,

302
00:14:12,537 --> 00:14:15,167
make sure your policy allows
it before you need it.

303
00:14:15,217 --> 00:14:17,427
And if you're still deciding
whether to buy a BYD,

304
00:14:17,477 --> 00:14:21,447
or any EV, ask the dealer three
questions before you sign.

305
00:14:21,497 --> 00:14:23,787
Where is the nearest
approved collision repairer?

306
00:14:23,837 --> 00:14:25,907
How long are service bookings right now?

307
00:14:25,957 --> 00:14:28,547
And are crash parts for this
model stocked in Australia?

308
00:14:28,597 --> 00:14:32,477
The answers will tell you a lot about
what your life looks like after a crash.

309
00:14:33,361 --> 00:14:36,911
So, is BYD's biggest problem
in Australia the car itself?

310
00:14:36,961 --> 00:14:37,731
Not really.

311
00:14:37,781 --> 00:14:41,271
The cars sell well and the battery
technology is genuinely good.

312
00:14:41,321 --> 00:14:43,511
The real challenge starts after the crash:

313
00:14:43,561 --> 00:14:46,811
a repair industry that's still
catching up with electric cars,

314
00:14:46,861 --> 00:14:48,351
a shortage of trained hands,

315
00:14:48,401 --> 00:14:50,091
insurers adjusting their prices,

316
00:14:50,141 --> 00:14:52,831
and a brand that grew faster
than its support network.

317
00:14:52,881 --> 00:14:56,771
The good news is that BYD is clearly
spending money to fix its side of it,

318
00:14:56,821 --> 00:14:59,971
with local parts, local batteries
and faster service targets.

319
00:15:00,021 --> 00:15:04,771
The question for 2027 is whether
repairers and insurers can keep up as

320
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:08,111
hundreds of thousands more of
these cars hit Australian roads.

321
